From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bas=20Magr=C3=A9?= <bas@opvolger.net>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:07:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] drm/amdgpu: Map the VRAM BAR uncached on non-coherent
 devices
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On the SpacemiT K1, CPU writes to VRAM through a write-combined
(RISC-V Svpbmt NC) BAR mapping can still be in flight when the doorbell
write reaches the GPU, so the GPU reads stale vertex/constant data,
visible as stretched triangles on the desktop.

Map the VRAM BAR uncached (Svpbmt IO, strongly ordered) on devices that
are not DMA-coherent, as the SpacemiT vendor kernel does.  Misaligned
user accesses to such a mapping need the access-fault emulation in
arch/riscv/kernel/traps.c.

Signed-off-by: Bas Magré <bas@opvolger.net>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_vram_mgr.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_vram_mgr.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_vram_mgr.c
index 249f07f30951..71490aec7363 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_vram_mgr.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_vram_mgr.c
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
+#include <linux/dma-map-ops.h>
 #include <linux/cgroup_dmem.h>
 #include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
 #include <drm/ttm/ttm_range_manager.h>
@@ -609,6 +610,18 @@ static int amdgpu_vram_mgr_new(struct ttm_resource_manager *man,
 
 	if (adev->gmc.xgmi.connected_to_cpu)
 		vres->base.bus.caching = ttm_cached;
+	else if (!dev_is_dma_coherent(adev->dev))
+		/*
+		 * On non-coherent platforms such as the SpacemiT K1, CPU writes
+		 * to VRAM through a write-combined (RISC-V Svpbmt NC) BAR mapping
+		 * can still be in flight when the doorbell (strongly ordered IO)
+		 * reaches the GPU, so the GPU reads stale vertex/constant data
+		 * (stretched triangles on the desktop).  Map the VRAM BAR
+		 * uncached (IO, strongly ordered) instead.  The SpacemiT vendor
+		 * kernel does the same for CONFIG_SOC_SPACEMIT_K1X.  Misaligned
+		 * user accesses to it are emulated, see arch/riscv/kernel/traps.c.
+		 */
+		vres->base.bus.caching = ttm_uncached;
 	else
 		vres->base.bus.caching = ttm_write_combined;
 
